														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4075289">
									

<p>I downvoted by the end of the first interview at the sight of some poorly-handled exposition. It didn't feel like a natural development of the conversation, rather, it gave the sense of trying to justify how the SCPF learned of a specific trait detailled in the Description.</p>
<p>Beyond that, the whole illogical and frighteningly cliche &quot;I am not a number&quot; exchange is the type of theatrics I eternally hope dies off for good for how rote it is typically in execution. It adds a needless level of melodrama to humanoid containment, and makes so little sense to think they'd dehumanize a humanoid like that on one hand, but also offer it therapy on the other.</p>
<p>I also feel there's probably a more sensible way to contain its effects beyond hand-wringing over Object Class and sticking it in a stronger room - hand/finger restraints seem like a logical go-to. If he can't articulate in order to grab something, he's incapable of accessing dangerous contraband.</p>
<p>Characterization, too, is a touch wonky: He's so good and righteous as to not attempt to kill his captors, but attempts escape using a lethal weapon?</p>
<p>I lost interest by the conclusion of the Incident Log: seeing another 6 or so collapsibles worth of content I was already having multiple issues with didn't inspire me to tread on.</p>
<p>And there's a number of &quot;it's&quot; mistakes that could stand correcting.</p>

							</div>

								
					
